<section id="glossary" class="panel">
 <div class="heading"><div class="kicker">11 / Study support</div><h2>Glossary & source notes</h2><p>Short definitions for technical terms used throughout the model.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
 <tr><td>ATP</td><td>Adenosine triphosphate; a molecule cells use to transfer usable energy.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>TCA cycle</td><td>Tricarboxylic acid cycle, also called the citric acid or Krebs cycle.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Oxidative phosphorylation</td><td>ATP production driven by the proton gradient generated by electron transport.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Aerobic glycolysis</td><td>High glycolytic activity with lactate production even when oxygen is available; commonly associated with the Warburg effect.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>PDH</td><td>Pyruvate dehydrogenase complex; converts pyruvate to acetyl-CoA.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>ROS</td><td>Reactive oxygen species; reactive oxygen-containing molecules that can participate in cell signaling or cause molecular damage.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Oncogene</td><td>A gene that can promote cell growth or survival when abnormally activated.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Hypoxia</td><td>A condition in which oxygen availability is lower than the tissue requires.</td></tr>
 <tr><td>Biosynthetic precursor</td><td>A molecule used as a starting material to build cellular components.</td></tr>
 </tbody></table></div>
